<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ansar (Sudan)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ansar ('helpers') were the followers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ahmad">Muhammad Ahmad</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, who rose against Turco-Egyptian rule in 1881. They destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-hicks">Hicks Pasha</a>'s army in 1883, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a> in 1885 and formed the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdist-state">Mahdist State</a> until its defeat in 1898. The name survives for the religious movement led by the Mahdi's descendants, the base of Sudan's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umma">Umma</a> Party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ansar-sudan.jpg" alt="Ansar (Sudan)" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muhammad_Ahmad_al-Mahdi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
